          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On the night of July 3rd to 4th, 1997 at 4:00 a.m., a witness observing from the deck of their sailboat saw a bright light descend rapidly for 2 to 3 seconds, stabilize for a moment, then quickly depart horizontally and disappear in approximately 2 to 3 seconds. The witness called their two sleeping crewmates to share their observation when they witnessed a second phenomenon, a yellow ocher diamond-shaped object with lights on its peaks. The object moved very quickly at cloud level and disappeared after 10 to 15 seconds. The observed phenomena remain unexplained.",
